<title>USA: FSA qualifies 10 muni issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies 10 muni issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance said it has qualified for bond insurance the following 10 municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>--Bonneville, Idaho, $7.4 million of general obligation jail bonds.</p>
<p>--Hesston, Kan., $2.93 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Bridgewater, Mass., $14.475 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Comstock Park Public Schools, Mich., $11.9 million.</p>
<p>--Greene CSD, N.Y., $5.4 million of school district bonds.</p>
<p>--Rush-Henrietta CSD, N.Y., $3.7 million of school district bonds.</p>
<p>--Springfield Township SD, Pa., $9.9 million GO bonds.</p>
<p>--Pickens Cty SD, S.C., $7 million GOs and $12 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Collierville, Tenn., $3.6 million of improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
